# The screen between the login and the desktop.
#
# This file exists because of what `startplasma` actually reads. It looks up
# `[KSplash] Theme` in ksplashrc and falls back to `org.kde.breeze` -- it does
# not consult the Look-and-Feel package the account is using. The Global Theme
# names the splash in its own `defaults` file, but that file is applied when
# somebody APPLIES the theme, and on a freshly installed machine nobody has:
# the account is created, the session starts, and the splash is whatever
# ksplashrc says. Without this line, that is Breeze's.
#
# This is the same shape as the wallpaper (ADR-091) and the battery percentage
# (ADR-110): the value was written in a file that is correct and that nothing
# on the first-login path reads.
#
# Either Look-and-Feel id would be right here, because both ship the same
# black splash since 2026-08-10 -- and that is worth stating rather than
# leaving as a coincidence, since it is why switching appearance does not need
# to touch this file.
#
# NOT YET CONFIRMED ON A RUNNING SESSION. The reasoning above comes from
# reading plasma-workspace, not from watching a machine, so the e2e's
# post-login block is where it gets settled.
[KSplash]
Theme=org.mimos.claro.desktop
